{
  "version": 5,
  "name": "How-Voltage-Works-Four-Step-Ladder-v3",
  "description": "A 12 volt supply feeds four 1 kilohm resistors in a row, so the voltage steps down 3 volts at each resistor. That puts the points between them at 9, 6, and 3 volts above ground (the 0 volt reference). Voltage is always measured between two points, so try different pairs with the multimeter: one resistor reads 3 volts, two in a row read 6, and the whole stack reads 12.",
